    <statement><p>Using the figure showing <m>f(x)</m> below, order the following
approximations to the integral <m>\int_0^3\,f(x)\,dx</m> and its exact
value from smallest to largest.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap7Sec5__Q13-image-1.png" width="33%"/>
<p><em>(Click on the graph for a larger version.)</em></p>
<p>Enter each of "LEFT(n)", "RIGHT(n)", "TRAP(n)", "MID(n)" and "Exact"
in one of the following answer blanks to indicate the correct
ordering:</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\lt </m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\lt </m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\lt </m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\lt </m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>RIGHT(n)</p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>MID(n)</p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>Exact</p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>TRAP(n)</p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>LEFT(n)</p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x)</m> to see how they over- or under- estimate the
area under the graph.  Here, 
<m>RIGHT(n)\lt MID(n)\lt Exact\lt TRAP(n)\lt LEFT(n).</m>



</solution>
